WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.590
This tulip photograph,
taken with a low-end camera,

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.510
exhibits a grayish look.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.970
We first manipulate its
large-scale component

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.580
to increase overall contrast.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.110
Note that this manipulation
only alters the tonal balance

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.340
while the amount of
texture remains the same.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.310
We can independently control
the amount of detail.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.570
This manipulation
preserves the tonal balance

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:41.445
that we just created.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.269
We can also provide a model
image such as this masterpiece

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:07.940
by Ansel Adams, and the
system automatically

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.910
transfers its multi-scale
characteristics.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.850
In comparison, a simple
pixel histogram matching

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.310
does not achieve the
appropriate texture level.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.040
The user can still
control the parameters

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.630
to finely tune the rendition.

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:07.460
Finally, the user can browse
previous working sessions

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.765
and predefined settings to
quickly explore various styles.

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:33.650
To better appreciate
our results,

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.440
we encourage you to consult
the prints in the accompanying

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.290
portfolio.

